aining day 10), then select fees matching merchant's profile + date-derived monthly stats, and also card scheme? Wait merchant's transactions on that day have card schemes; \"applicable to merchant\" may mean union over the merchant's transactions on that day of rules that match each transaction. Then \"For the 10th\" specifically because they filter payments to that date. Why not say \"in January\" then? Q1753 says \"in March 2023\" (whole month). So likely Q1681 filters payments by `day_of_year = 10` (a single day), and computes monthly volume/fraud? The monthly volume could be for that merchant in that month (Jan) regardless of day. Then applicable fees are union of rules applicable to transactions on day 10. Q1753 filters March all transactions, union over month. That makes wording consistent.\n\nSimilarly Q1871 \"In January 2023 what delta would Belles pay...\" uses all Jan transactions. Q2697 \"For Belles in January...\" all Jan.\n\nWe need know whether fee application per transaction is unique or average/all. Let's see if per-transaction union with monthly bands yields many zero-match transactions. If questions 1681/1753 ask \"applicable fee IDs\" maybe they don't care that all transactions have a fee; they just collect rules matching merchant + transaction attributes, maybe only for transactions where rules exist. But zero-match means those transactions have no applicable fee rule; okay.\n\nLet's compute union of applicable fee IDs for Jan 10 transactions and March under matching all non-null including transaction attrs and monthly bands. Also union for all Jan. See counts, differences."}
{"type": "tool_call", "callId": "call_00_2XIVAgqHqzhQ1C3DmFgt0323", "tool": "bash", "input": {"command": "python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,csv,datetime,collections\nfees=json.load(open('inputs/fees.json'))\nmd={m['merchant']:m for m in json.load(open('inputs/merchant_data.json'))}\ndef vmatch(v,val):\n    if v is None: return True\n    if isinstance(v,list): return len(v)==0 or val in v\n    return str(v)==str(val)\ndef applicable(r,mer,volband,fraudband):\n    out=[]\n    intra=1.0 if r['issuing_country']==r['acquirer_country'] else 0.0\n    credit=r['is_credit']=='True'\n    for f in fees:\n        if f['card_scheme'] is not None and f['card_scheme']!=r['card_scheme']: continue\n        if not vmatch(f['account_type'],mer['account_type']): continue\n        if f['capture_delay'] is not None and f['capture_delay']!='<3': continue\n        if f['monthly_volume'] is not None and f['monthly_volume']!=volband: continue\n        if f['monthly_fraud_level'] is not None and f['monthly_fraud_level']!=fraudband: continue\n        if not vmatch(f['merchant_category_code'],mer['merchant_category_code']): continue\n        if not vmatch(f['is_credit'],credit): continue\n        if not vmatch(f['aci'],r['aci']): continue\n        if f['intracountry'] is not None and float(f['intracountry'])!=intra: continue\n        out.append(f['ID'])\n    return out\ndef band(v,bands):\n    for name,(lo,hi) in bands.items():\n        if lo<=v<hi: return name\n    return None\nfraudbands={'<7.2%':(0,7.2),'7.2%-7.7%':(7.2,7.7),'7.7%-8.3%':(7.7,8.3),'>8.3%':(8.3,999)}\nvolbands={'<100k':(0,100000),'100k-1m':(100000,1000000),'1m-5m':(1000000,5000000),'>5m':(5000000,1e18)}\nrows=collections.defaultdict(list)\nstats=collections.defaultdict(lambda:{'vol':0.0,'fraud':0.0})\nwith open('inputs/payments.csv') as f:\n    for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n        if r['merchant']!='Belles_cookbook_store': continue\n        d=int(r['day_of_year']); m=(datetime.date(2023,1,1)+datetime.timedelta(d-1)).month\n        rows[m].append(r); stats[m]['vol']+=float(r['eur_amount'])\n        if r['has_fraudulent_dispute']=='True': stats[m]['fraud']+=float(r['eur_amount'])\nfor m in [1,3]:\n    v=stats[m]['vol']; fr=100*stats[m]['fraud']/v\n    print('month',m,v,fr,band(v,volbands),band(fr,fraudbands))\nfor label,rr,m in [('jan10',[r for r in rows[1] if int(r['day_of_year'])==10],1),('jan',rows[1],1),('mar',rows[3],3)]:\n    v=stats[m]['vol']; fr=100*stats[m]['fraud']/v\n    ids=set(); nomatch=0\n    for r in rr:\n        a=applicable(r,md['Belles_cookbook_store'],band(v,volbands),band(fr,fraudbands))\n        if not a: nomatch+=1\n        ids.update(a)\n    print(label,'tx',len(rr),'ids',len(ids),'nomatch',nomatch,'sorted',sorted(ids))\nEOF", "description": "Union applicable IDs for day/month interpretations"}}
