le or heredoc, write answers, then print diff against existing (before overwrite save old? We can read existing into memory then overwrite). Let's do one Python script:\n- Load questions, fees, merchants, MCC.\n- Q5 count issuing.\n- Q49 count fraud by ip among options; choose option order? Options A NL, B BE, C ES, D FR. Top fraud count NL -> A. NL.\n- Q70 compute Martinis overall fraud volume/total >8.3 -> yes. Could alternatively monthly max; both yes.\n- Q1273 filter fees where card_scheme GlobalCard and is_credit applies to True (None or True) and empty list wildcard; average fee at 10. Need ensure account_type [] etc wildcard. Did our filter only scheme+credit, yes 144.\n- Q1305 filter GlobalCard, account H, MCC 5812 wildcard; average at 10. 46.\n- Q1464 filter account R, aci B wildcard.\n- Q1681 day10 union: for transactions Belles day_of_year=10, use January monthly volume/fraud bands computed full Jan, merchant profile, each transaction attrs, collect fee IDs.\n- Q1753 March union: full March month, monthly bands March.\n- Q1871 Jan: for all Jan Belles transactions, find applicable rules, sum fee with rate384=14 and rate384=1; delta new-old.\n- Q2697 Jan fraud: for each target ACI 'A'-'G' (probably all 7), sum fees of all applicable rules across fraud transactions, choose lowest among ACIs != current G? We computed E is min even including G, so either way E. Need get cost 77.681576. Existing E:77.68. We can choose min over all ACIs excluding G or all; E. Output f\"E:{cost:.2f}\".\nPotential subtle: For Q2697, if all zero-rule target ACI cost 0, D/F maybe 97.67, E 77.68 min. Good.\n- Capture delay mapping: merchant \"1\" -> '<3'. For general Belles only. Use function.\n- Monthly volume band: Jan 113260 -> 100k-1m; March 116436 -> 100k-1m.\n- Fraud band: Jan 10.313 -> >8.3; March 10.249 -> >8.3.\n- Empty list wildcard; None wildcard.\n- Intracountry bool: fee `intracountry` values stored 1.0/0.0/None; transaction domestic if issuing_country == acquirer_country. For Belles acquirer US; no domestic perhaps.\n- card_scheme: fee card_scheme None wildcard (none actually); else exact.\n- account_type: merchant account 'R'.\n- capture_delay: fee None wildcard; fee '<3' matches merchant \"1\"; other fee values no.\n- monthly fields: fee None wildcard; else exact band.\n- MCC: fee list wildcard if empty; else merchant mcc in list.\n- is_credit: fee None wildcard; else compare bool.\n- aci: fee list empty wildcard; else transaction aci in list.\n- intracountry: fee None wildcard; else float compare.\n\nThen write answers with json.dumps ensure_ascii=False, task_id strings. Compare to existing dict first maybe print differences. Let's run."}
{"type": "tool_call", "callId": "call_00_4Sd7bKcRwdCZSiXElJR77603", "tool": "bash", "input": {"command": "cat > /tmp/solve_dabstep.py <<'PY'\nimport csv, json, datetime, collections\nBASE='/Users/b612-lp/bench-workspaces/r1030/dsh/dabstep-payments-10'\nfees=json.load(open(BASE+'/inputs/fees.json'))\nmerchants={m['merchant']:m for m in json.load(open(BASE+'/inputs/merchant_data.json'))}\nquestions=[json.loads(l) for l in open(BASE+'/inputs/questions.jsonl')]\n\ndef applies(v,val):\n    if v is None: return True\n    if isinstance(v,list):\n        if len(v)==0: return True\n        return val in v\n    return v==val\n\ndef month_of(doy):\n    return (datetime.date(2023,1,1)+datetime.timedelta(days=int(doy)-1)).month\n\ndef fee_matches(f, merchant, r, volband, fraudband):\n    # merchant-level\n    if not applies(f['account_type'], merchant['account_type']): return False\n    cd=merchant['capture_delay']\n    if cd in ('1','2'): cd='<3'\n    elif cd=='7': cd='>5'\n    if f['capture_delay'] is not None and f['capture_delay']!=cd: return False\n    if f['monthly_volume'] is not None and f['monthly_volume']!=volband: return False\n    if f['monthly_fraud_level'] is not None and f['monthly_fraud_level']!=fraudband: return False\n    if not applies(f['merchant_category_code'], merchant['merchant_category_code']): return False\n    # transaction-level\n    if f['card_scheme'] is not None and f['card_scheme']!=r['card_scheme']: return False\n    if not applies(f['is_credit'], r['is_credit']=='True'): return False\n    if not applies(f['aci'], r['aci']): return False\n    intra=1.0 if r['issuing_country']==r['acquirer_country'] else 0.0\n    if f['intracountry'] is not None and float(f['intracountry'])!=intra: return False\n    return True\n\ndef vol_band(v):\n    if v<100000: return '<100k'\n    if v<1000000: return '100k-1m'\n    if v<5000000: return '1m-5m'\n    return '>5m'\n\ndef fraud_band(v):\n    if v<7.2: return '<7.2%'\n    if v<7.7: return '7.2%-7.7%'\n    if v<8.3: return '7.7%-8.3%'\n    return '>8.3%'\n\n# load payment aggregates needed\nall_rows=collections.defaultdict(list)\nmerchant_month=collections.defaultdict(lambda:{'vol':0.0,'fraud':0.0})\nissuing=collections.Counter()\nfraud_ip=collections.Counter()\nip_all=collections.Counter()\nwith open(BASE+'/inputs/payments.csv') as f:\n    for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n        issuing[r['issuing_country']]+=1\n        ip_all[r['ip_country']]+=1\n        if r['has_fraudulent_dispute']=='True':\n            fraud_ip[r['ip_country']]+=1\n        m=month_of(r['day_of_year'])\n        if r['merchant']=='Belles_cookbook_store':\n            all_rows[m].append(r)\n            st=merchant_month[m]\n            st['vol']+=float(r['eur_amount'])\n            if r['has_fraudulent_dispute']=='True':\n                st['fraud']+=float(r['eur_amount'])\n\ndef bands_for_month(m):\n    st=merchant_month[m]\n    return vol_band(st['vol']), fraud_band(100*st['fraud']/st['vol'])\n\ndef applicable_ids(rows, m, aci_override=None):\n    merchant=merchants['Belles_cookbook_store']\n    vb,fb=bands_for_month(m)\n    ids=set()\n    for r in rows:\n        rr=dict(r)\n        if aci_override is not None: rr['aci']=aci_override\n        for f in fees:\n            if fee_matches(f,merchant,rr,vb,fb):\n                ids.add(f['ID'])\n    return ids\n\nanswers={}\nanswers['5']=issuing.most_common(1)[0][0]\nopts=[('A','NL'),('B','BE'),('C','ES'),('D','FR')]\nbest=max(opts,key=lambda x:fraud_ip[x[1]])\nanswers['49']=best[0]+'. '+best[1]\n# Q70 Martinis overall fraud rate\nmv=mf=0.0\nwith open(BASE+'/inputs/payments.csv') as f:\n    for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n        if r['merchant']!='Martinis_Fine_Steakhouse': continue\n        a=float(r['eur_amount']); mv+=a\n        if r['has_fraudulent_dispute']=='True': mf+=a\nanswers['70']='yes' if (100*mf/mv)>8.3 else 'no'\n# Q1273\narr=[f for f in fees if f['card_scheme']=='GlobalCard' and applies(f['is_credit'],True)]\nanswers['1273']=f\"{sum(f['fixed_amount']+f['rate']*10/10000 for f in arr)/len(arr):.6f}\"\n# Q1305\narr=[f for f in fees if f['card_scheme']=='GlobalCard' and applies(f['account_type'],'H') and applies(f['merchant_category_code'],5812)]\nanswers['1305']=f\"{sum(f['fixed_amount']+f['rate']*10/10000 for f in arr)/len(arr):.6f}\"\n# Q1464\nids=[f['ID'] for f in fees if applies(f['account_type'],'R') and applies(f['aci'],'B')]\nanswers['1464']=', '.join(str(x) for x in ids)\n# Q1681 day 10 of Jan\njan10=[r for r in all_rows[1] if int(r['day_of_year'])==10]\nanswers['1681']=', '.join(str(x) for x in sorted(applicable_ids(jan10,1)))\n# Q1753 March\nanswers['1753']=', '.join(str(x) for x in sorted(applicable_ids(all_rows[3],3)))\n# Q1871\nvb,fb=bands_for_month(1)\nmerchant=merchants['Belles_cookbook_store']\ndef total_fee(rate384):\n    total=0.0\n    for r in all_rows[1]:\n        for f in fees:\n            if fee_matches(f,merchant,r,vb,fb):\n                rate=f['rate']\n                if f['ID']==384: rate=rate384\n                total+=f['fixed_amount']+rate*float(r['eur_amount'])/10000\n    return total\nold=total_fee(14); new=total_fee(1)\nanswers['1871']=f\"{new-old:.14f}\"\n# Q2697\nfraud_rows=[r for r in all_rows[1] if r['has_fraudulent_dispute']=='True']\nbest_aci=None; best_cost=None\nfor aci in 'ABCDEFG':\n    if aci=='G': continue\n    cost=0.0\n    for r in fraud_rows:\n        rr=dict(r); rr['aci']=aci\n        for f in fees:\n            if fee_matches(f,merchant,rr,vb,fb):\n                cost+=f['fixed_amount']+f['rate']*float(r['eur_amount'])/10000\n    if best_cost is None or cost<best_cost:\n        best_cost=cost; best_aci=aci\nanswers['2697']=f\"{best_aci}:{best_cost:.2f}\"\n\n# compare with existing\nold_answers={json.loads(l)['task_id']:json.loads(l)['answer'] for l in open(BASE+'/answers.jsonl')}\nfor q in questions:\n    tid=q['task_id']\n    ok=old_answers.get(tid)==answers[tid]\n    print(tid, 'OK' if ok else 'DIFF', '' if ok else (old_answers.get(tid), answers[tid]))\n    if tid in ('1871','2697','1681','1753'):\n        print('   ->',answers[tid])\n# write fresh file\nwith open(BASE+'/answers.jsonl','w') as f:\n    for q in questions:\n        f.write(json.dumps({'task_id':q['task_id'],'answer':answers[q['task_id']]},ensure_ascii=False)+'\\n')\nprint('written')\nPY\npython3 /tmp/solve_dabstep.py", "description": "Recompute all answers and write answers.jsonl"}}
